WEBVTT

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:05.320
The chain or crochet cast-on is a very
useful technique for machine knitters.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.854
It doesn't have as much stretch as some
methods, but it is good when you want

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.040
to match your cast-on to your bind-off
for scarves and blankets, for example.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.680
Start by forming a slip
knot over your latch tool.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.360
Place the tool between the first two
needles on the left side of the bed.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.440
Position the yarn from the mast
on the left of the first needle.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.960
Reach up and catch the yarn
in the hook of the tool.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.080
Pull down and pull the newly formed loop
through the loop on the tool.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.254
Holding the new loop in place,
put the tool between

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.940
the second and third needle.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.320
And repeat this procedure
across all of the needles.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:14.934
When you reach the end of the needles
in work, secure the last

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.640
loop on the last needle.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.120
You'll notice that by just chaining on the
needles, it's difficult to hang weights.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.800
A cast-on comb would solve this problem,
but a cast-on comb isn't always available.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:47.280
Try starting with waste
yarn and ravel cord first.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.720
Or try using a cast on rag.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:55.280
I'm using a swatch from a previous
project and hanging it on the needles.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.640
There's no need to be neat and tidy,
you'll be removing this later.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:06.120
After the rag is on the needles, knit one
row of ravel cord and hang the weights.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.080
I've pulled all the needles
out to make the cast on easier.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.040
You'll now chain cast-on
over all the needles.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.480
When you remove the work from the machine,
you can easily pull out the ravel

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.480
cord and remove the cast-on rag.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:03.880
This technique can be done any machine,
and you'll have a beautiful chain edge.

